  outside:{chapter:'Chapter I · A Thin Red Line',title:'The hunger underneath',place:'Port Mercy · Rainline District',image:'photo-1524665989156-7790a6df972f',caption:'Rainline District · The old quarter',text:`<p>Cold rain brings the city into focus. Port Mercy rises in layers: old brick, neon, church spires disappearing into fog. Your reflection in a shop window looks almost like you.</p><p>A woman in a red coat waits beneath the awning. She introduces herself as Mara Voss, and says she has been looking for you since before you died. Across the street, a cab idles with its lights off.</p>`,speaker:'MARA VOSS',choices:[['A','Hear Mara out.','She seems to know what you are.'],['B','Take the cab.','Trust no one; find your own answers.'],['C','Ask where you can feed.','The hunger is getting louder.']]},
  mara:{chapter:'Chapter I · A Thin Red Line',title:'The house with no mirrors',place:'Port Mercy · Voss House',image:'photo-1511895426328-dc8714191300',caption:'The Voss House · Somewhere in the city',text:`<p>Mara's townhouse is older than its neighbors and twice as quiet. No mirrors. No clocks. She offers a glass of dark red wine, untouched, and explains the rules: don't draw eyes, don't leave bodies, and never trust a promise made before sunrise.</p><p>Tonight, someone called the Grey Choir has stolen a ledger from the old Rialto Theatre. It contains the names of everyone who has gone missing this month. Mara wants it back. She wants to know why you were found at the scene.</p>`,speaker:'MARA VOSS',choices:[['A','Accept the job.','The ledger could tell you who made you.'],['B','Demand the truth first.','You weren’t born yesterday.'],['C','Refuse—and look for the Choir alone.','You don’t take orders.']]},
- theatre:{chapter:'Chapter II · The Grey Choir',title:'Music for the newly dead',place:'Port Mercy · Rialto Theatre',image:'photo-1519608487953-e999c86e7455',caption:'The Rialto · Curtains at midnight',text:`<p>The Rialto's marquee has been dark for twenty years. Tonight, a low cello note vibrates through its locked doors. A narrow side entrance stands ajar. Inside, someone moves between the seats, humming a hymn you almost remember.</p><p>You can feel three heartbeats beyond the curtain. One quick and terrified. Two slow, steady, and utterly calm.</p>`,speaker:'',choices:[['A','Slip in unseen.','Let the dark hide you.'],['B','Walk through the front doors.','Make them decide if you’re a threat.'],['C','Use your new gift to listen.','Blood remembers what ears cannot.']]},
